    "failure_scenario": "The pool drains to zero at every session boundary: session N+1's first agent call cannot start until session N's last result is consumed and its serial reconcile agent calls (one per facty chunk, not prefetched) finish. After preprocessing strips tool I/O, most sessions fit in one 48 KB chunk, so a backlog of 200 single-chunk sessions issues exactly one agent call at a time — concurrency=4 buys zero overlap precisely in the common case the feature targets (hours of latency-bound calls). Cheaper: a run-wide worker pool fed chunks from upcoming sessions (chunking/preprocessing is independent of consumption), or at minimum start session N+1's prefetch while session N's tail is being consumed; ordered consumption per session is preserved either way."
